      },
      "worked": "Two distinct edges lie in a plane if they are parallel or meet at a vertex.\n\nThere are three edge directions, each containing four parallel edges. Thus the number of parallel pairs is\n$$3\\binom{4}{2}=18.$$\nAt each of the eight vertices, three edges meet. Each intersecting pair is counted at exactly one vertex, so the number of intersecting pairs is\n$$8\\binom{3}{2}=24.$$\nThese cases are disjoint. Therefore, the number of pairs is\n$$18+24=42.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
